Janis Papanagnou wrote:
> OTOH, it was never apparent to me why the separate "play the right tune"
> disclosure while praying would be of any use; first it's rare to get - why
> not just provide the second, i.e. the full disclosure "here's the tune"
> message. IMO, the first message is something for the Oracle chit-chat and
> fortune cookie's contents than a divine present. And the second message is
> as well not really worth the effort; after all you can always play the game
> of Mastermind to open the drawbridge.

Presumably the first message is intended for an unspoiled player.
Without it, you'd never think to play an instrument to open the
drawbridge, but if you know that much, you might be able to guess
that it's a mastermind game by trying a few different combinations.
Then the second message is just an extra hint if you couldn't figure
that out.

And while it would seem to be appropriate for a major consultation,
keep in mind that most players aren't going to buy too many of those,
and there's no guarantee that they'll get the specific hint.  But
hardly anyone will make it all the way to the castle without praying
enough to get the hint.  Not that it's completely necessary, since you
can always go in the back...

Alternately, it could serve the same purpose for prayer as most of the
foo-bane weapons do for sacrifice: keep the player from actually
getting something useful too early/often.



